{
  "_comment": [
    "Which tests a change runs. Read by Scripts/select_tests.py (CI's plan job) and Scripts/check_ui_shards.py.",
    "ui_shards: the XCUITest split. Every UI test method must be selected by exactly one shard. minutes is the shard's measured CI job time (median, setup included); the plan queues the longest first, so refresh it when a shard's contents change. allowance is how many seconds one test may run before XCTest fails it (default 300). retry false runs a failing test once instead of twice (default true; the nightly never retries).",
    "smoke_shard: added to every run that selects any UI shard.",
    "ui_classes_by_target: for each module the app links, the UI test classes its changes run; \"all\" runs every shard. select_tests.py --check fails when a UI class spells out an accessibility identifier a module defines and the module's list does not name it.",
    "ui_shared_support: UI test files every UI test launches through; a change to one runs every shard. Any other UI test file runs its own classes and every class whose file uses a type it declares.",
    "full_paths: a change here runs every unit suite and every UI shard.",
    "release_paths: a change here also runs the Release build, which otherwise runs only nightly and on a manual full run.",
    "gallery_paths: debug-only gallery code no UI test reaches; a change here runs gallery_unit_targets and no UI shard.",
    "path_owners: source a target compiles from outside its buildable folder, with that target.",
    "snapshot_paths: when a pull request push changes only these, and the previous head passed the UI suite, that verdict stands and no UI shard runs again.",
    "linux_only_paths: a change here needs no macOS job; the Linux job always runs.",
    "cli_paths: a change here runs the macOS build and CLI end-to-end checks without unit or UI tests.",
    "This file: a change confined to ui_shards runs the shards it adds or changes; a change to anything else runs everything.",
    "Any path matched by none of these and owned by no Tuist target runs everything, the Release build included."
  ],
